{"title":"Treatment Planning Assistant Roadmap","role":"Treatment Planning Assistant","summary":"A Treatment Planning Assistant supports the radiotherapy team in preparing and organizing information required for safe and accurate radiation-treatment planning. The role typically works under the direction of radiation oncologists, medical physicists and qualified radiation-therapy professionals.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Radiotherapy Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Treatment Planning Assistant supports the radiotherapy team in preparing and organizing information required for safe and accurate radiation-treatment planning. The role typically works under the direction of radiation oncologists, medical physicists and qualified radiation-therapy professionals."},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the institution and qualification, responsibilities may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Preparing patient and treatment-planning records"},{"text":"Assisting with CT-simulation workflow"},{"text":"Organizing imaging and treatment data"},{"text":"Supporting contouring and planning workflows under supervision"},{"text":"Entering patient-specific treatment information"},{"text":"Maintaining treatment-planning documentation"},{"text":"Coordinating between radiation oncology, physics and therapy teams"},{"text":"Supporting quality-assurance documentation"},{"text":"Assisting with treatment-plan checks within defined scope"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is a highly safety-sensitive healthcare field. A Treatment Planning Assistant should not independently prescribe radiation dose, approve treatment plans, interpret medical images, or perform duties reserved for qualified radiation oncologists or medical physicists."},{"type":"p","text":"For advanced treatment-planning roles, specialized radiotherapy/medical-radiation technology education and institutional authorization may be required."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Focus","Key Capabilities"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Radiation & healthcare foundations"},{"text":"Anatomy, physiology, radiation basics"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Radiotherapy technology"},{"text":"Simulation, immobilization, treatment workflow"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Planning fundamentals"},{"text":"CT datasets, dosimetry concepts, planning systems"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Clinical integration"},{"text":"Planning support, QA, patient safety"}],[{"text":"0–2 Years"},{"text":"Planning / Radiation Therapy Trainee"},{"text":"Workflow support"}],[{"text":"2–4 Years"},{"text":"Treatment Planning Assistant"},{"text":"Planning-system support"}],[{"text":"4–7 Years"},{"text":"Senior Planning / Therapy Professional"},{"text":"Complex workflow coordination"}],[{"text":"7+ Years"},{"text":"Planning / Radiation Oncology Operations Lead"},{"text":"Technical and operational leadership"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year-Wise Learning Plan"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Medical & Radiation Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Basic oncology"},{"text":"Radiation physics fundamentals"},{"text":"Radiation biology"},{"text":"Healthcare ethics"},{"text":"Patient safety"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Learn the basics of"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cancer types"},{"text":"Tumour biology"},{"text":"Radiation treatment principles"},{"text":"External beam radiotherapy"},{"text":"Brachytherapy"},{"text":"Radiation safety"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical documentation"},{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Healthcare teamwork"},{"text":"Computer literacy"},{"text":"Excel"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Radiotherapy Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiotherapy workflow"},{"text":"CT simulation"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Immobilization"},{"text":"Treatment machines"},{"text":"Linear accelerator fundamentals"},{"text":"Treatment accessories"},{"text":"Radiation protection"},{"text":"Image-guided radiotherapy concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment awareness"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand the purpose of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT simulator"},{"text":"Linear accelerator"},{"text":"Treatment couch"},{"text":"Immobilization devices"},{"text":"Imaging systems"},{"text":"Treatment-planning systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical exposure"},{"type":"h","text":"Observe the complete workflow:"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"CT Simulation"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Acquisition"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Planning"},{"type":"h","text":"Plan Verification / QA"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Delivery"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Monitoring"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Treatment Planning Fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Planning concepts"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Treatment-planning principles"},{"text":"CT image datasets"},{"text":"Patient coordinate systems"},{"text":"Target volumes"},{"text":"Organs at risk"},{"text":"Dose concepts"},{"text":"Dose-volume histograms"},{"text":"Beam arrangements"},{"text":"Treatment techniques"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment techniques"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop conceptual knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D conformal radiotherapy"},{"text":"IMRT"},{"text":"VMAT"},{"text":"IGRT"},{"text":"SRS"},{"text":"SBRT"},{"text":"Brachytherapy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Planning software"},{"type":"p","text":"Gain supervised familiarity with the concepts behind:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Treatment Planning Systems (TPS)"},{"text":"DICOM"